meta {
  name: Submit Attempt
  type: http
  seq: 9
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/student/assessments/attempts/{{assessmentAttemptId}}/submit
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
}

docs {
  Student-initiated early submit: "in_progress" -> "completed" ->
  immediately "under_evaluation" (every attempt needs an evaluator
  review/publish step, even if fully auto-scored). Same terminal
  transition the auto-submit job uses for its graceful (duration/window
  expiry) path.

  At finalization, any autoScorable question the student never submitted
  a response for gets an explicit StudentAnswer row auto-created with
  autoScore/finalScore: 0 and evaluation_status: "auto_scored" (i.e.
  scored wrong) — same as an incorrect answer, just without negative
  marking (nothing was actually chosen to penalize). Unanswered
  non-autoscorable (subjective) questions are left alone and still wait
  for manual evaluation. This applies to every path through finalize():
  student submit, the auto-submit job's duration/window-expiry path, and
  the tab-hidden termination path.
}
